admapOverviewCard` needs to generate the HTML for displaying the roadmap overview. It iterates through each stage, calculating stage statistics to determine completion status and progress. I'll need to use these stats to dynamically render the item's appearance, including a bullet, title, progress bar, and focus tag for the current stage. The `escapeHTML` function is used for preventing Cross-Site Scripting (XSS).\n\n\nThe `renderRoadmapOverviewCard` function is being constructed to display the roadmap. It iterates through each learning stage using the provided statistics. The completion status of each stage (\"not\\_started\", \"in\\_progress\", or \"mastered\") is determined based on problem counts, solved problem counts, completion percentage, and milestone status. The HTML structure includes the stage number, title, progress bar, and visual indicators for completion status. The active stage is highlighted with a focus banner, displaying solved/total problems and a \"Continue\" button. The function leverages an existing `escapeHTML` function for data sanitization.\n\n\nAggregate statistics across all stages are computed to track overall progress. Stages are filtered according to a `roadmapFilter` value, which can be 'in\\_progress', 'mastered', or 'not\\_started'. The quick jump navigation bar items are built to show stage status. Status icons are set based on stage completion.\n\n\nStatus icons for the quick jump navigation are being set based on stage completion status; a relevant icon is selected depending on whether the stage is in progress. The generation of roadmap stage cards is underway, with completion status dynamically applied to each card for visual clarity. Active focus highlights are rendered based on the active stage. The code now iterates through the roadmap data to create a structured display.\n\n\nThe roadmap overview card generation is now producing HTML, using calculated stage statistics. Completion status badges are rendered dynamically based on computed statistics (mastered, in progress, not started).  Topic chips are being added to each stage card. Action buttons for setting stage focus and indicating the active stage are incorporated.\n\nHTML for the roadmap overview cards is now complete, including dynamic progress bars, completion status indicators, descriptions, and key concept displays. The `escapeHTML` function is implemented to prevent XSS vulnerabilities.  I'm verifying all display components are rendering correctly with the calculated statistics.\n\n\nHTML is being generated for each stage, including a progress bar reflecting solved problems and difficulty distribution. A milestone banner is constructed, dynamically showing milestone problem name, solving status, and a button linking to the workspace.\n\nThe roadmap cards now incorporate recommended starter problems, offering users a quick access point to start practice. The overall structure is complete, and now I'm inspecting the rendered output to verify accuracy.\n\n\nThe HTML for the roadmap cards includes recommended starter problems for each stage. I'm dynamically generating the HTML for each starter problem chip, including badges for difficulty and LeetCode number, along with the problem title and pattern. Visual indicators for solved or attempted status are also included. Action buttons are added to open a full workspace. Currently, I'm inspecting the output for accuracy.\n\n\nThe roadmap overview card now renders HTML for each stage. It incorporates a progress bar reflecting problem-solving progress and difficulty distribution. A milestone banner is included, which shows the milestone problem's status and links to a workspace.\n\nThe roadmap cards feature recommended starter problems for quick practice initiation.  Dynamic HTML generation for each starter problem chip is implemented, along with difficulty and LeetCode number badges. Visual indicators and workspace action buttons are also included.\n\n\nThe generated HTML for the roadmap overview card now incorporates starter problems within each stage. I am dynamically producing the starter problem chips, including difficulty and LeetCode badges. Visual cues and buttons for workspace interaction are also integrated. The rendering of these components is under review.\n\n\nOverall progress statistics are calculated across all stages. The roadmap now includes quick jump navigation with stage status icons.  Roadmap cards are being generated dynamically, reflecting stage completion.\n\nDynamic completion status application is being applied to each roadmap card, enhancing the visual clarity. The code is structured to iterate through the data to create a display.\n\nThe HTML for each roadmap card is being generated, using calculated statistics.  Completion status badges and topic chips are being included. Action buttons for stage focus are also incorporated.\n\n\nThe full roadmap and the roadmap timeline-only views are being rendered, and statistics are computed. The `renderRoadmapTimelineOnly` function is implemented to update a specific container with the full roadmap view using the computed stats. The code verifies `DsaDashboard` and other relevant data are exposed to the global `window` object.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html","EndLine":90,"StartLine":50,"toolAction":"Viewing tab buttons in index.html","toolSummary":"View tab buttons in index.html"}}]}
